66	\subsection*{Ambient plane and constants}
67	
68	\begin{definition}[Scattering plane, dot product, and perpendicular bracket]
69	\label{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:Plane}
70	\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.Plane}
71	\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.dot}
72	\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.perp}
73	The ambient centre-of-mass plane $\mathrm{Plane} = \mathbb{R}^2$ (the
74	Euclidean space on $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$) on which the relative motion lives,
75	with the standard scalar product $\langle v, w\rangle = v_x w_x + v_y w_y$
76	and the oriented planar bracket $\mathrm{perp}\ v\ w = v_x w_y - v_y w_x$ --
77	the signed $z$-component of the 2D cross product, positive exactly when $w$
78	is reached from $v$ by a counterclockwise rotation of less than
79	$180^{\circ}$.  The bracket carries the rotation sense of the deflection
80	(branch/orientation bookkeeping) and the planar angular momentum.
81	\end{definition}
