88	\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.elementaryCharge}
89	\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.bohrRadius}
90	The fixed physical constants, kept abstract (opaque) so that nothing about
91	the target can be obtained by unfolding: the inertial mass $m$ of each
92	particle (electron and positron, kg), the reduced Planck constant $\hbar$
93	(J\,s), the Coulomb constant $k = 1/(4\pi\varepsilon_0)$
94	(N\,m$^2$\,C$^{-2}$), the elementary charge
95	magnitude $e$ (the electron carries $-e$, the positron $+e$; C), and the
96	Bohr radius $a_0 = 4\pi\varepsilon_0\hbar^2/(m e^2) = \hbar^2/(k m e^2)$
97	(m).
98	\end{definition}
