389	Any asymptotic relative velocity satisfies
390	$\lVert u_\infty \rVert = \sqrt{2E/m_{\mathrm{red}}}$ and
391	$\mathrm{angleBetween}\ \hat u_0\ u_\infty
392	= \arctan\!\big(1/\sqrt{\varepsilon^2 - 1}\big)$.
393	Contains the sign/orientation input but no numeric deflection value.
394	(Iter-014 repair: the previous conclusion
395	$\pi - 2\arctan(1/\sqrt{\varepsilon^2-1})$ was the apocenter-referenced
396	Rutherford expression; for this periapsis-referenced scenario (the
397	recorded instant is the periapsis,
398	\cref{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:turningQuadratic_periapsis})
399	the tangent at periapsis is perpendicular to the symmetry axis, so the
400	angle at the initial line of motion is the complementary acute angle
401	$\arctan(1/\sqrt{\varepsilon^2-1})$ --- the official reading
402	$\theta = 90^\circ - \arccos(-1/\varepsilon)$, with
403	$\arccos(-2/7) = 106.60^\circ$ the angle taken from the $y$-axis.)
404	\end{theorem}
405	\begin{proof}
406	The magnitude follows from the energy law at infinity, where the Coulomb
407	term vanishes and $E = \tfrac12 m_{\mathrm{red}} \lVert u_\infty \rVert^2$.
408	For the direction, the hyperbola of
409	\cref{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:orbit_eq_conic} with
410	$\varepsilon > 1$ has asymptote directions making the acute angle
411	$\arccos(1/\varepsilon) = \arctan\sqrt{\varepsilon^2 - 1}$ with the
412	symmetry axis; the initial line of motion at periapsis is perpendicular to
413	that axis (radial speed zero,
414	\cref{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:turningQuadratic_periapsis}),
415	so the acute angle between the initial line and the outgoing asymptote is
416	$\pi/2 - \arccos(1/\varepsilon)
417	 = \arctan\!\big(1/\sqrt{\varepsilon^2 - 1}\big)$, read off on the
418	branch side recorded in
419	\cref{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:IsAsymptoticRelativeVelocity}.
420	\end{proof}
